# A campaign keeps its stale registration (the rule of `MatchStep::
# StaleConfiguration`, review of #132): when the matchmakers' histories
# name a reconfiguration to another configuration, the candidate runs its
# leadership under the configuration it registered, not under the
# effective one. A reconfiguration that removed members is rolled back,
# and a leadership waits on members that left or are gone.
expect: caught
cause: matchmaking: a completed campaign runs the effective configuration
cause: matchmaking: a completed ordinary campaign registered the effective configuration
file: crates/lib/paros-core/src/node/matchmaking.rs
--- find
            .filter(|(newest, config)| *newest > floor || honored.as_ref() == Some(config))
--- replace
            .filter(|(newest, config)| false && (*newest > floor || honored.as_ref() == Some(config)))
--- end
